== Shiitake Dashi ==

First make the @shiitake dashi{2%cups}. (While this is cooking you can prepare the vegetables)

== Ankake Sauce ==

After the dashi is ready and while still hot add @mirin{2%Tbsp}(microwaved 20-30 secs to reduce alcohol), @light soy sauce{2%Tbsp} and stir in.

Next gradually add the @potato starch{1 1/2%Tbsp} in @water{3%Tbsp} slurry into the dashi mixture stirring continuously to avoid clumping. Bring to a gentle boil and within ~{1%minute} or so, the mixture should be noticeably thicker. Once thickened remove from heat and cover. This is your ankake (sauce)

== Vegetables ==

Use a large #sauté pan{} on medium heat, add in the @extra virgin olive oil{1-2%Tbsp} and cook the @renkon{1/2%piece}(quartered 1/4 in thick) and @fresh shiitake mushrooms{1 1/2%cups}(sliced 1/4 in thick) for ~{1-2%minutes}. Add in the @aburaage{2%pieces}, @red bell pepper{1/4}(sliced 1/4 in thick), @yellow bell pepper{1/4}(sliced 1/4 in thick), @sugar snap peas{1/2%cup}, and @enoki mushrooms{1/2%bunch}(bottom part removed) and cook ~{4-5%minutes} until softened. Stir occasionally and allow to brown slightly.

Once the vegetables have softened add all the ankake sauce to the vegetable pan and mix the vegetables into the sauce. Remove from heat.

== Serving ==

Place one serving of brown rice into a large #bowl{} and pour the vegetable ankake sauce over the rice ~ about 1 cups worth.

Top with desired herbs or peppers and enjoy!

> You can substitute sesame oil for the olive oil.